WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.675
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:09.536
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.836 --> 00:00:15.983
Unit seven: Negative Sentences (don't/doesn't). Today you will say what is not true with don't and doesn't.

4
00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:18.842
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.917
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.494
Don't.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.204
Don't means short for do not.

8
00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:29.201
I don't like coffee.

9
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:32.202
Your turn. Say: Don't.

10
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:35.766
Don't.

11
00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:37.286
Doesn't.

12
00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:40.132
Doesn't means short for does not.

13
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.101
She doesn't eat meat.

14
00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:44.893
Your turn. Say: Doesn't.

15
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:48.514
Doesn't.

16
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.030
Not.

17
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.550
Not means a word that makes a sentence negative.

18
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.407
He is not here.

19
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:58.530
Your turn. Say: Not.

20
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.426
Not.

21
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:04.080
Negative.

22
00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:08.058
Negative means saying no or that something is not true.

23
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.696
A negative sentence uses not.

24
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.576
Your turn. Say: Negative.

25
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:17.307
Negative.

26
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:18.935
I don't.

27
00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.334
I don't means I do not.

28
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:22.835
I don't know.

29
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.882
Your turn. Say: I don't.

30
00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:29.595
I don't.

31
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.421
She doesn't.

32
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:34.207
She doesn't means she does not.

33
00:01:34.817 --> 00:01:36.038
She doesn't play.

34
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.175
Your turn. Say: She doesn't.

35
00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:42.976
She doesn't.

36
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:44.474
Never.

37
00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:47.297
Never means not at any time.

38
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:49.117
I never lie.

39
00:01:49.717 --> 00:01:53.251
Your turn. Say: Never.

40
00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:56.939
Never.

41
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:58.371
No.

42
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:01.302
No means the opposite of yes.

43
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:03.057
No, thank you.

44
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.059
Your turn. Say: No.

45
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.680
No.

46
00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:14.303
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.779
Visal, do you like spicy food? You can say 'I don't like spicy food.'

48
00:02:20.883 --> 00:02:28.568
Yes! I don't like spicy food. We use don't with I, you, we and they. We use doesn't with he, she and it.

49
00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:31.660
What comes after don't or doesn't?

50
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:40.989
The base verb, without s. She doesn't play, not 'she doesn't plays'. The s moves to doesn't, so the main verb stays simple.

51
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:43.700
Is there any other way to say no?

52
00:02:44.783 --> 00:02:54.433
Yes. Never means not at any time. I never eat meat. We also use not with be: I am not tired. They are not here.

53
00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:56.951
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.817 --> 00:03:01.987
Grammar focus: Negatives: don't and doesn't plus base verb.

55
00:03:02.287 --> 00:03:03.428
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.489
I don't like coffee.

57
00:03:06.383 --> 00:03:07.698
She doesn't eat meat.

58
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:09.735
They don't live here.

59
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:17.149
Use don't with I, you, we and they, and doesn't with he, she and it. After both, use the base verb without s.

60
00:03:17.883 --> 00:03:21.255
Be careful! Don't say: She doesn't likes tea.

61
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.130
Say: She doesn't like tea.

62
00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.464
Use the base verb after doesn't.

63
00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:31.302
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.333
Things I Don't Do.

65
00:03:33.633 --> 00:03:36.028
I don't drink coffee, but my father does.

66
00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.370
My sister doesn't like spicy food.

67
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.308
We don't go to school on Sunday.

68
00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.207
My cat never eats vegetables.

69
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.966
A negative sentence uses not, don't or doesn't.

70
00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:54.115
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.288
She blank like rain.

72
00:03:56.588 --> 00:03:59.893
A, don't. B, doesn't. C, isn't.

73
00:04:03.433 --> 00:04:05.897
The answer is B: doesn't.

74
00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.084
They blank play football on Monday.

75
00:04:09.384 --> 00:04:12.318
A, don't. B, doesn't. C, not.

76
00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:17.448
The answer is A: don't.

77
00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:20.188
I blank know the answer.

78
00:04:20.488 --> 00:04:23.561
A, doesn't. B, am not. C, don't.

79
00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.821
The answer is C: don't.

80
00:04:29.983 --> 00:04:31.553
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:31.853 --> 00:04:36.621
A, He doesn't plays.. B, He doesn't play.. C, He don't play..

82
00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.816
The answer is B: He doesn't play..

83
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.913
According to the reading, who doesn't like spicy food?

84
00:04:47.213 --> 00:04:51.122
A, my father. B, my sister. C, my cat.

85
00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.782
The answer is B: my sister.

86
00:04:57.967 --> 00:05:01.037
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:01.883 --> 00:05:05.148
Write one negative sentence using 'don't' and one using 'doesn't'.

88
00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.613
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:15.913 --> 00:05:29.345
I don't eat fish, and my brother doesn't eat eggs. We use don't with I and doesn't with he, she or it. After them we use the base verb. This is how I make a negative sentence in the present simple.

90
00:05:29.645 --> 00:05:31.354
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:37.619
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and negatives: don't and doesn't plus base verb.

92
00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:41.105
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

93
00:05:41.405 --> 00:05:43.779
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

94
00:05:44.079 --> 00:05:46.650
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

